### Tier 1 marketplace demo — REST Client requests
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and run requests top-to-bottom.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@sellerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@buyerId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@adminId  = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
@widgetId    = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
@gizmoId     = bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb
@doohickeyId = cccccccc-cccc-cccc-cccc-cccccccccccc

### 1) Seller creates a product   (use case: CreateProduct)
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Seller
X-User-Id: {{sellerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sample Widget", "price": 15.00, "stock": 25 }

### 5) Buyer lists published products   (use case: ListProductsForBuyer)
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}

### 2) Buyer places an order with sufficient stock — 201 Created, Confirmed
# @name placeOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{widgetId}}", "quantity": 2 }

### 2b) Buyer places an order with insufficient stock — 422, persisted as Failed
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{doohickeyId}}", "quantity": 1 }

### 3) Buyer cancels their own order — stock returns   (use case: CancelOrder)
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}

### 6) Admin lists ALL products, including any future drafts   (use case: ListProductsForAdmin)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/products
X-User-Role: Admin
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### Place another order so admin can force-cancel it
# @name secondOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{gizmoId}}", "quantity": 3 }

### 4) Admin force-cancels any order — stock returns   (use case: ForceCancelOrder)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orders/{{secondOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
X-User-Role: Admin
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### Wrong role — buyer trying a seller endpoint returns 403
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
X-User-Role: Buyer
X-User-Id: {{buyerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Naughty", "price": 1.00, "stock": 1 }
